# SABOTAGE: T84b (ADR-044 s7.3, RP-J-8b - the row the first draft's ranked ladder got wrong).
# Samen.Fleet.Directive.Precedence.local_off?/2's rollout_pct <= 0 clause is what makes
# "fleet is a one-way OFF authority" hold even when a local operator disabled a flag via
# rollout_pct: 0 rather than the kill switch. Dropping it means a fleet directive with
# rollout_pct: 100 SILENTLY RE-ENABLES a flag a local operator zeroed out during an incident -
# exactly the hole this predicate exists to close. Positive control: local KILL
# (enabled: false) still correctly forces local_off? true (untouched clause).
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/fleet_directive_precedence_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: local rollout_pct: 0 beats fleet rollout_pct: 100 (the case the ranked ladder got wrong)
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/directive/precedence.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/directive/precedence.ex
index 630d4f4..ee4bec5 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/directive/precedence.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/directive/precedence.ex
@@ -69,7 +69,6 @@ defmodule Samen.Fleet.Directive.Precedence do
   @spec local_off?(local_config(), map()) :: boolean()
   def local_off?(local_config, subject) when is_map(local_config) and is_map(subject) do
     not truthy?(get(local_config, :enabled)) or
-      rollout_pct(local_config) <= 0 or
       local_rule_off?(local_config, subject)
   end
 
